      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.1 Definition of Computer"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Computers are defined by specific basic functions and foundational characteristics.",
        "Computers are categorized into three primary types: Analog, Digital, and Hybrid.",
        "The evolution of computer technology is mapped across distinct Generations of Computers.",
        "Understanding computer fundamentals and classifications is essential for competitive exam preparation."
      ],
      "id": "x6fcbrq"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gro55p1",
      "content": "A computer is an electronic device that takes raw data as input, processes it using programs, stores the data, and produces output in the form of information."
    },
